A||||3||RacinRob||85 Gt,  A couple of questions||||5||
Z||000000||RacinRob||03-25-2001||03:54 PM||||First my spedo bounces around, or did... I would be going down the road a 30 mph and it would bounce up to 45, down to 20 all over the place. It has stopped doing it since I buried the needle, but I'm afraid it will come back.<BR>Second, I want to paint some of the interior panels, but I love Armoral does anyone know how to get this stuff off without hurting the plastic.  After the Armoral is off should I paint the stuff with primer first...? I'm painting the silver panels BTW.<P>Third, my check engine light is coming on after the car is warmed up, code 14 and 44 which are IAC and lean exhaust O2. The car idles wonderful and doesn't seem to have any problems so, will it hurt the car to ignore theses codes.<P>Forth, I am thinking about starting a webpage with the subject of fast American car... I'm really sick of imports around here so I figured I should do something... is there any interest in a webpage like this or does anyone know of a site like this. it would just feature tricked out American cars.  <P>Fifth, I love the forum and I am learning a lot, I am new to fieros, kinda.  I bought my brothers after he bought a 3000gt VR-4.  He had a 85 se and 85 GT that I have been working on for the 5 years that he owned them, but now it is my turn to see what I can do with it.   <P>Thanks for the info.||||reg||5
Z||000001||FieroJoe||03-25-2001||07:34 PM||||Welcome to the Forum!<P>I can give you some ideas about the interior painting.  You are right in thinking you really need to get the armor all off.  Thought I havent done it before, I think mineral spirits (paint thinner) should be able to do the job without damaging the plastic.<P>Yes, use primer first!  A good primer will adhere to the plastic well and provide a good base for your final coat.  I would reccomend scuffing up the plastic pieces just a little bit even before you prime, use maybe 800 grit sandpaper, and remember to lightly sand in between all coats of paint!<P>I hope that helps.<P>btw:  I remember reading about the speedo problem a few times, but I cant remember what the fix was, try searching on it, I bet you'll find at least one thing.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||03-26-2001||01:55 AM||||At least replace the O2 sensor. Its not that hard to replace. You can take out the IAC and spray some cleaner to see if its just jammed up with carbon. If not just replace it.<P>Ignoring lights now have a way of kicking your ass when you least need it!||||reg||4
Z||000003||GoCartGuy||03-26-2001||09:48 AM||||Answer to your painting question.  To get the Armorall off use acetone.  Its safe on almost all surfaces interior with the exception of the black plastic trim (around cig lighter, door latches and the base around power window switches).  Using it on these deteriorates the surface...you'll notice the cloth with turn black.  Other than that yea a good primer is a must.  Just my two cents, I'm doing my interior now.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
